WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.625
Porter's five forces explain why some industries make more money than others.

00:00:04.675 --> 00:00:09.896
Rivalry, new entrants, substitutes, the power of buyers and the power of suppliers.

00:00:09.946 --> 00:00:12.538
Strong forces squeeze margins.

00:00:13.233 --> 00:00:15.424
Bottled water feels all five.

00:00:15.474 --> 00:00:19.657
Rivals everywhere, anyone can launch one, and tap water is free.

00:00:19.707 --> 00:00:22.367
So most brands fight on price.

00:00:23.067 --> 00:00:25.965
Then Liquid Death built a brand nobody could copy.

00:00:26.015 --> 00:00:29.657
Buyers happily paid more, and rivals were locked out.

00:00:30.367 --> 00:00:31.543
Use it like this:

00:00:31.593 --> 00:00:32.947
rate each force high,

00:00:32.997 --> 00:00:34.256
medium or low,

00:00:34.306 --> 00:00:35.364
find the strongest,

00:00:35.414 --> 00:00:38.077
and show how the brand can weaken it.
